<title>UK: British Airways ground staff back strike.</title>
<headline>British Airways ground staff back strike.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON</dateline>
<text>
<p>A second group of workers at British Airways Plc approved strike action Monday as ground workers voted to strike in protest against the airline's decision to sell off its catering unit.</p>
<p>The ground staff's vote, which followed last week's decision by cabin crew who overwhelmingly voted for industrial action in a bitter five-month dispute over pay and working conditions, increased the likelihood of disruption of flights.</p>
<p>The Transport and General Workers Union said 62.5 percent of its members who voted approved of the strike action.</p>
</text>
